Here's a table which I know I emailed you before, but I'm not sure I ever 
posted:

==========
If you're interested in spellcasting, it is important to keep 
"difficulty" at or below zero by gaining levels and advancing spell 
skills.  This table shows the needed XL at each combination of spell 
level and spell skill:

 Spell Level   Unskilled       Basic        Skilled        Expert 
------------------------------------------------------------------
      1            -             -             -             -    
      2          XL  9           -             -             -    
      3          XL 21         XL  3           -             -    
      4            +           XL 15           -             -    
      5            +           XL 27         XL  9           -    
      6            +             +           XL 21         XL  3  
      7            +             +             +           XL 15  

A plus sign means that the spell will always have a positive 
"difficulty", even at XL 30.  A minus sign means that even an XL 1 
character would have a zero or negative "difficulty".  (Technically, an 
XL 1 character is not able to advance spell skills anyway)
==========

